    "text": " def parse_iso8601(s: str) -> datetime:\n       try:\n           if s[-1] == 'Z':\n               return datetime.fromisoformat(s[:-1])\n           elif '+' in s or '-' in s:\n               return datetime.fromisoformat(s)\n           else:\n               dt = datetime.fromisoformat(s)\n               return dt.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n       except ValueError:\n           raise ValueError(\"Invalid ISO-8601 timestamp\")\n\n   # Examples\n   print(parse_iso8601('2022-03-01T15:30:00Z'))  # UTC\n   print(parse_iso8601('2022-03-01T15:30:00+05:00'))  # Explicit offset\n   print(parse_iso8601('2022-03-01T15:30:00'))  # Naive timestamp (UTC)\n   try:\n       print(parse_iso8601('invalid_timestamp'))  # Raises ValueError\n   except ValueError as e:\n       print(e)",
